Type 'help' for help
(sdb) help
List of commands:
  append          Append a value to a variable: append $<var> += <value>
  backtrace       Show the backtrace of template calls (alias: bt): backtrace [full]
  break           Add a breakpoint, optionally conditional: break [loc] [if expr]
  callflow        Enable/Disable call flow tracing: callflow [on | off]
  clear           Clear a watchpoint watch variable: clear [$var | num]
  condition       Set, change, or clear a breakpoint's condition: condition <num> [expr]
  continue        Continue running the script: continue [loc]
  delete          Delete all (or one) breakpoints: delete [num]
  down            Move the selected frame toward the innermost frame: down [n]
  dump            Dump internal information about libxml2 objects: dump [<options>]
  finish          Finish the current template
  help            Show this help message: help [cmd ...] [all]
  info            Showing info about the script being debugged: info [<options>]
  list            List contents of the current script: list [loc]
  locals          List contents of local variables
  next            Execute the over instruction, stepping over calls
  over            Execute the current instruction hierarchy
  print           Print the value of an XPath expression: print <xpath>
  profile         Profiler subcommand: profile [<options>]
  reload          Reload the script contents
  run             Restart the script
  set             Set a variable to a new value: set $<var> = <value>
  step            Execute the next instruction, stepping into calls
  tbreak          Add a temporary breakpoint, deleted when hit: tbreak [loc] [if expr]
  up              Move the selected frame toward the outermost frame: up [n]
  verbose         Turn on verbose (-v) output logging
  watch           Set a watchpoint on a variable: watch variable $var
  where           Show the backtrace of template calls (alias: bt)
  quit            Quit debugger

Command name abbreviations are allowed
(sdb) help profile
List of command under 'profile':
    on              Enable profiling
    off             Disable profiling
    clear           Clear profiling information
    callgraph       Enable callgraph profiling, writing output to <file>
    flamegraph      Enable flame-graph profiling, writing output to <file>
    brief           Report profiling information, briefly
    wall            Report profiling information, wall-clock
    report          Report profiling information [brief | wall | callgraph | flamegraph] [<file>]
(sdb) help info
List of command under 'info':
    breakpoints     Display current breakpoints
    insert          Display current insertion point
    files           Display open files (imports, includes)
    output          Display output document
    locals          Display local variables
    profile         Report profiling information: info profile [brief | wall]
    watch           Display current watchpoints
